## Description

This week on ThursdAI: Anthropic's Claude Code 512K lines of source code accidentally leaked via NPM — and the internet went wild. We break down the hidden features (Kairos daemon mode, anti-distillation, buddy system), the session gate billing crisis, and the fastest GitHub repo ever (144K stars) with guest Sigrid Jin.

Google DeepMind's Omar Sanseviero joins live to announce Gemma 4 — four open-weight models under Apache 2.0 license, with a 31B dense model competing with 1T+ parameter models on LM Arena. We discuss agentic capabilities, local inference, and why Gemma is the new Llama.

Plus: OpenAI's insane $122B funding round, Microsoft AI's new transcription/voice/image models, Prism ML's mind-blowing 1-bit quantization (8B model in 1GB!), Wolf Bench proving Hermes beats Claude Code as an agent harness, and Anthropic's research on emotion vectors inside Claude.

